  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="bc79-4d3c-5f56-100c" name="Sumerian (Armies of Antiquity) - List Notes" publicationId="aab0-aa1e-0319-4ffe" hidden="false">
      <description>SUMERIAN ARMY LIST (Armies of Antiquity, pp.2-3), Sumerian and Akkadian armies, c.3000-2000 BC.
Characters: the army may have a General and an Army Standard Bearer. Chariotry up to a quarter of the points; Infantry at least a quarter; Allies &amp; Tribal Mercenaries up to a quarter.
Special rules: Throw sticks (same effect as a javelin) and Onagers (see the rule).

ARMY COMPOSITION (percentages by points):
  Chariotry: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Allies &amp; Tribal Mercenaries: up to 25%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
